+- Projection (`src/engine/fastled/fastledProjection.ts`, deck section "FastLED" in `FastLedProjectionPanel.tsx`): *index* keeps `leds[i]` → map index i and passes `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS` = map pixel count; *surface* compiles without PXLBLZ defines (the sketch keeps its NUM_LEDS) and gives the handle a precomputed table map index → sketch LED (−1 = black), so `render*(i)` emits the L2/L1 bytes of `table[i]` and the packed frame keeps the map's pixel count (router frame size unchanged). Sketch positions: the sketch's screen maps (`getScreenMaps()`, host export `pxl_screenmap_json`, sent by the worker with `started`/changed frames; serpentine/XYMap already applied), else the catalogue `geometry` width×height row-major (serpentine when the source declares `kMatrixSerpentineLayout = true`/`SERPENTINE true`; a clone finds its example by the provenance header), else a square guess with a deck notice. Map positions: each pixel's `sample` (2D: x,y; 3D: chosen axis pair, default the two largest extents), fitted onto the sketch bounds padded by half an LED (Contain: uniform scale, whole map inside the sketch; Fill: per axis), optional flips; nearest sketch LED within one LED pitch via a bucket grid, ties → lower index; memoised per (map points, sketch layout, options), ~ms for 10,330 pixels. Automatic choice: surface for `@pxlblz-dim` ≥ 2 on a ≥2D map unless the source uses `PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS/WIDTH/HEIGHT` or the known LED count (catalogue, or after start) equals the map's. Persistence: `// @pxlblz-projection [index|surface] [fit=fill] [flip=x|y|xy] [axes=xy|xz|yz]` in an editable Pattern's header; the compile request blanks that line and the artifact cache key drops it, so a projection change never recompiles. Read-only examples store the same text as `fastledProjection` in their `demoOverrides` bag (cleared by "Revert to recommended"); Clone writes it into the copy's header.
+- Preview start: the deck pauses itself while no Pattern is loaded (upstream #478); it now resumes when the pause was automatic and a Pattern arrives (cold load, deep link), while a user pause stays.
 - Controls: FastLED UI elements map to ranged slider/toggle Controls (`PatternMetadata.controls[].range`); values persist in `PatternRecord.controls` (`controls_json`) keyed by UI name.
 - Worker and watchdog: the worker runs the same host calls in the same order, so bytes are identical; frames are pipelined by one IDE frame (frame(dt_k) requests frame k while frame k-1 is shown; a late answer repeats the last frame and the deltas accumulate). No answer within 2 s (setup 10 s) terminates the worker: runtime error, last frame kept. The host's loop/show budget still reports runaway loops that call `millis/delay/show` (they keep running). Measured at 4,593 LEDs: ~1 ms per frame in the worker, ~1.4 ms round trip, main-thread cost ~0.1 ms per frame; added latency one IDE frame.
-- Limits: catalogue examples use the stock layouts (square grids match their XY size; ring/free screen-map geometry is not yet a preview map). Compiler failures caused by the machine (out of memory) are not cached. Playlists (sequencing Pixelblaze and FastLED Patterns with cuts/crossfades) are a planned follow-up.
+- Limits: catalogue examples use the stock layouts (square grids match their XY size); on other maps the surface projection samples their screen map. A screen map changed after the first frame is not re-read until the preview rebuilds. Compiler failures caused by the machine (out of memory) are not cached. Playlists (sequencing Pixelblaze and FastLED Patterns with cuts/crossfades) are a planned follow-up.
 
